
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.CreateKeyValue(Key: string, Value: string): uuid`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`key llCreateKeyValue(string Key, string Value);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Start an asynchronous transaction to create a key-value pair associated with the script&#39;s <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Experience" target="_blank">Experience</a> using the given key (<b>k</b>) and value (<b>v</b>).</p>
  <p>Returns a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Key/handle" target="_blank">handle</a> (a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Key" target="_blank">key</a>) that can be used to identify the corresponding <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Dataserver" target="_blank">dataserver</a> event to determine if this command succeeded or failed.</p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>string</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>string</span></td>
          <td>Key / k</td>
          <td>The key for the key-value pair</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>string</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>string</span></td>
          <td>Value / v</td>
          <td>The value for the key-value pair. Maximum 2047 characters, or 4095 if using Mono.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>data_storage</li>
        <li>dataserver</li>
        <li>experience</li>
        <li>experience_data</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">387</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-experience">Experience</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <p>If the key already exists the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Dataserver" target="_blank">dataserver</a> will return a failure along with the error <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/XP_ERROR_STORAGE_EXCEPTION" target="_blank">XP_ERROR_STORAGE_EXCEPTION</a>.</p>
  <p>As of Jan 1, 2016 maximum bytes is 1011 for key and 4095 for value for both LSO and Mono scripts.</p>
  <p>For this function to work, the script must be compiled into an <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Experience" target="_blank">Experience</a>.</p>
  <h2>Specification</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Maximum memory storage: 128 MiB</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Dataserver</p>
  <p>The <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Dataserver" target="_blank">dataserver</a> callback parameters are:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A key containing the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Key/handle" target="_blank">handle</a> returned from llCreateKeyValue</li>
    <li>A string containing a comma-delimited list (<b>cdl</b>). `llDumpList2String([ [integer](https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Integer) **success** ] + **components**);`
    <ul>
      <li><b>components</b> vary depending upon success or failure of request.</li>
      <li>Failure: `**cdl** = [llDumpList2String](https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlDumpList2String)([ 0, [integer](https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Integer) **error**],&quot;,&quot;)`</li>
      <li>Success: `**cdl** = [llDumpList2String](https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlDumpList2String)([ 1, [string](https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/String) **value** ],&quot;,&quot;)`</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>String Components</p>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>• integer</td>
        <td><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Integer/boolean" target="_blank">success</a></td>
        <td>–</td>
        <td>A boolean specifying if the transaction succeeded (1) or not (0).</td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>• integer</td>
        <td><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Integer/experience_error" target="_blank">error</a></td>
        <td>–</td>
        <td>An <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Integer/experience_error" target="_blank">XP_ERROR_*</a> flag that describes why the operation failed.</td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>• string</td>
        <td>value</td>
        <td>–</td>
        <td>The value for the key-value pair. Maximum 2047 characters, or 4095 if using Mono. Note! This value may contain commas.</td>
        <td></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If you recompile a script that was previously associated with an Experience but do so with a client that lacks the ability to compile scripts into an experience the script will lose the associated Experience.</li>
    <li>It is recommended that keys do not contain commas due to <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlKeysKeyValue" target="_blank">llKeysKeyValue</a> returning keys in CSV format.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

local function integer(s) return tonumber(string.match(s, "^%s*([-+]?%d+)")) or 0 end

local trans = NULL_KEY
function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local total_number = #events
    trans = ll.CreateKeyValue("FOO", "BAR")
end

function LLEvents.dataserver(t, value)
    if t == trans then
        -- our llCreateKeyValue transaction is done
        local result = integer(ll.GetSubString(value, 0, 0))
        if result == 1 then
            -- the key-value pair was successfully created
            ll.Say(0, "New key-value pair was created")
        else
            -- the key-value pair was not created
            local error = integer(ll.GetSubString(value, 2, -1))
            ll.Say(0, "Key-value failed to create: " .. ll.GetExperienceErrorMessage(error))
        end
    end
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`key trans;
default
{
    touch_start(integer total_number)
    {
        trans = llCreateKeyValue("FOO", "BAR");
    }



    dataserver(key t, string value)
    {
        if (t == trans)
        {
            // our llCreateKeyValue transaction is done
            integer result = (integer)llGetSubString(value, 0, 0);
            if (result == 1)
            {
                // the key-value pair was successfully created
                llSay(0, "New key-value pair was created");
            }
            else
            {
                // the key-value pair was not created
                integer error = (integer)(llGetSubString(value, 2, -1));
                llSay(0, "Key-value failed to create: " + llGetExperienceErrorMessage(error));
            }
        }
    } 
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <p>Compiling</p>
  <p>For a script to be associated with an <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Experience" target="_blank">Experience</a>...</p>
  <ul>
    <li>It must be compiled with a client that is Experience aware,</li>
    <li>The &quot;Use Experience&quot; checkbox must be checked,</li>
    <li>And one of the users Experience keys selected.</li>
  </ul>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td></td>
        <td><b>Important:</b> Not all <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/TPV" target="_blank">TPVs</a> have this functionality.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
